# Cloudflare Workers Deployment

Deploy target: **Cloudflare Workers** via `@opennextjs/cloudflare` (not static export).

## Build pipeline

```bash
npm run build       # opennextjs-cloudflare build
npm run preview     # local Worker preview
npm run deploy      # build + deploy to Cloudflare
```

Config: `open-next.config.ts`, `wrangler.jsonc`.

## Runtime model

- **No** `output: 'export'` — full Next.js SSR on Workers
- Fetch Sanity content server-side in Server Components (`src/lib/sanity/productStore.js`)
- Use `export const revalidate = 60` on content pages for ISR-like caching
- `nodejs_compat` flag enabled in wrangler

## Environment (set in Cloudflare dashboard + `.env.local`)

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=sfqhf74q
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=   # optional, for private datasets
```

## Safety checklist

- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds
- [ ] Sanity fetch works on Worker (no Node-only APIs at runtime beyond OpenNext compat)
- [ ] No `export const runtime = 'edge'` in source files
- [ ] Static assets cached via `public/_headers`
